            <chunk name="Object" index="225">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">049a7fb4-2178-4be0-a440-e59f1fcc3b73</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">This is a 5 step process for defining Information for the XR Assembly.

STEP 8: Select Robot
   - As Compas XR defines specific robots currently the following robots are the only ones acceptable for visualization
   - "UR3", "UR5", "UR10e", "ETHZurichRFL"
   - If a custom or specific robot is added on the application side this can be updated by following
     the documentation.

STEP 9: Set Compas XR Publisher &amp; Subscriber &amp; Options
   - As the messaging process can be customized based on specific requirements &amp; the application expects messages on 
     specific topic names the following information needs to be provided to send and receive information on the 
     application side.

   - host: Any MQTT Broker (Default is hive.broker.mq) but allows customization for private brokers etc.
   - project_name: The project name that you uploaded information for on firebase. Additionally this is in the 
     specification of messaging topics, so it is important that you use the specific topic name as assembly.
   - robot_name: informs the application of which robot is being planned for.

STEP 10: Set Compas XR Planning Request Subscriber
    - This is a simple process, but is important that it happens before requesting a trajectory from the application.

    - On: Bool: Initilizes the component.
    - Reset: Bool: Initilizes the subscription.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="5">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>982</X>
                          <Y>36</Y>
