                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">This Section includes a 4 Step Process that is primarily defined by the Compas_Fab library, and is used to define planning sequences that can be visualized from the Application.

NOTE: ALL PLANNING SEQUENCES ARE JUST EXAMPLES, AND SHOULD BE DEFINED SPECIFIC TO THE PROJECTS ASSEMBLY STRATEGY.

STEP 11: Load the robot from ROS
    - Loads the specified Robot from ROS as instructed.
    - ex. This can be done using `docker_compose.yml` files or through connecting to the specific ROS node.

STEP 12: Attach tool to the Robot.
    - This is done using compas fab and allows for any custom tool attachment.

STEP 13: Update Collision Meshes from Built Objects.
    - This is done simply through Compas Fab, but has been adjusted to work with the Compas XR Library.

STEP 14: Transform Selected Part &amp; Place Frame
    - Additionally this component has been customized to work with this specific example.
    - It works by transforming the slected part to the required location and passing its information to the requested element.
    - Additionally it transforms the selected parts frame to the place frame. 
     (This can be handled in a multitude of ways &amp; should be tailored for your assembly process)

STEP 15: Define Robotic Planning Strategy - Custom for specific project.
    - This is done through the Compas Fab Library, and in this case has been defined for a simple pick and place routine.
    - It includes a 4 Step Process: Solve Inverse Kinemeatics &amp; Trajectory for Pick, Solve Inverse Kinematics for Place &amp; Approach Place, &amp; Plan Trajectories for Place &amp; Move Trajectory.
    - NOTE: THIS PROCESS IS ONLY AN EXAMPLE, AND SHOULD BE CUSTOMIZED FOR EACH PROJECT SPECIFICALLY.</item>
                  </items>
