            <chunk name="Object" index="237">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">689a5902-1163-45da-b2c8-2198686877b1</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">This Section includes a 2 Step Process for Defining &amp; Publishing Trajectory Responses.

STEP 17: Combine Trajectories &amp; Base Frame Definition
    - Trajectory Combination: As the application requires a single trajectory for visualization. 
    - The trajectory combination component simply combines all individual trajectories into one single trajectory.
    - Additionally it defines the pick index by taking the length of the pick_trajectory.

    - Base Frame Review: Due to the inconsistency in URDF structures. The component for base frame review was simply added to ensure 
      correct visualization on the application side.
    - This rotation may not be needed for some URDF objects, but should be reviewed based on the project.

STEP 18: Publish Trajectory Result.

    SYNC RESULT
    - element_id: (string) Is the requested items step ID.
    - Trajectory: (compas_robots.JointTrajectory) The combined trajectory that is wished to be visualized. 
       - NOTE: if trajectory is null message can still be published and the application will be notified accordingly.
    - robot_base_frame: (compas.geometry.Frame) Used to position the robot in space in relation to the structure.
    - pick_and_place: (bool)(Optional) Is used to notify the application the trajectory is intended to attach the object.
    - pick_index: (int)(Optional) Informs the app when the item is attached in the trajectory.
    - ee_link_name: (str)(Optional) Informs the application to which link the object is attached.

    PLANNING RESULT PUBLISH:
    - Options: Compas XR Options (same as previous component)
    - Result: Trajectory Planning Result
    - Publish: (bool) Publish the result.
</item>
                  </items>
